Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThere exist constants $c_2,$ $c_1,$ and $c_0$ such that\n\\[x^3 + x^2 - 5 = (x - 3)^3 + c_2 (x - 3)^2 + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0.\\]Find $c_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"461bdd88a6b14346e3bb9b0a0dd1ab15e81edab6484ecd77a1dde789df9ef4aa"},"seconds":47.402791261672974,"seed":543751022075079870,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for the constants $c_2,$ $c_1,$ and $c_0$ in the equation\n\\[x^3 + x^2 - 5 = (x - 3)^3 + c_2 (x - 3)^2 + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0,\\]\nwe first need to expand the right-hand side and match the coefficients with the left-hand side polynomial $x^3 + x^2 - 5$.\n\nStart by expanding $(x-3)^3$:\n\\[\n(x-3)^3 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27.\n\\]\n\nNext, expand $c_2 (x-3)^2$:\n\\[\nc_2 (x-3)^2 = c_2 (x^2 - 6x + 9) = c_2 x^2 - 6c_2 x + 9c_2.\n\\]\n\nThen, expand $c_1 (x-3)$:\n\\[\nc_1 (x-3) = c_1 x - 3c_1.\n\\]\n\nFinally, $c_0$ remains as it is:\n\\[\nc_0.\n\\]\n\nCombine all these expansions:\n\\[\n(x-3)^3 + c_2 (x-3)^2 + c_1 (x-3) + c_0 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27 + c_2 x^2 - 6c_2 x + 9c_2 + c_1 x - 3c_1 + c_0.\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\nx^3 + (-9 + c_2)x^2 + (27 - 6c_2 + c_1)x + (-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0).\n\\]\n\nMatch the coefficients with $x^3 + x^2 - 5$:\n1. Coefficient of $x^3$: $1 = 1$\n2. Coefficient of $x^2$: $1 = -9 + c_2 \\Rightarrow c_2 = 10$\n3. Coefficient of $x$: $0 = 27 - 6c_2 + c_1 \\Rightarrow 0 = 27 - 6(10) + c_1 \\Rightarrow c_1 = 33$\n4. Constant term: $-5 = -27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0 \\Rightarrow -5 = -27 + 9(10) - 3(33) + c_0 \\Rightarrow -5 = -27 + 90 - 99 + c_0 \\Rightarrow -5 = -36 + c_0 \\Rightarrow c_0 = 31$\n\nNow we have $c_2 = 10$, $c_1 = 33$, and $c_0 = 31$. Calculate $c_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2$:\n\\[\nc_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2 = 10^2 + 33^2 + 31^2 = 100 + 1089 + 961 = 2150.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2150}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2150}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
